export
Usage: export NAME=VALUE  |  export NAME

Shell builtin. Mark a variable so that programs the shell starts inherit
it. Without export a variable exists only inside the shell itself.

	export TERM=linux
	export PATH="$PATH:/opt/bin"
	export		list everything currently exported

vos's init exports HOME, TERM and the XDG_* paths this way before it
hands you a shell.

See also: set, unset, read
